by taking kids and randomly assigning them to art education or non-art education and looking at improvement over a year, there was nothing. So we came out with a paper called Mute Those Claims, no evidence yet for transfer. And transfer of learning from one area to another has been notoriously hard to prove in psychology. People used to think that learning Latin made you more logical. Well, that's been shown not to be right. Learning Latin makes you better at Latin.

