personal meanings in their work. So observation, expression, reflection, engagement. They're learning to be very engaged, to stick to things over time. These are big, broad habits of mind, which we think are very important to have. They can be taught in any subject, but we think they're often best talk in art classrooms with a studio atmosphere and with critiques. And so we had a book, we wrote a book called Studio Thinking, The Real Benefits of Visual Arts Education, and we're now coming out with our third edition. And we also wrote one called Studio Thinking from the start,

